YASD and YAAD are such appropriate acronyms, don't you think? "Yet
Another" certainly does express an appropriate frustration at being
killed by a vengeful RNG, a couple of ants, a newt and a floating eye,
or worse yet, by a stupid newbie mistake.

We all know how you folks love to share your own stories about your
exploits down in the Mazes of Menace, so in the interest of self-
promotion and the sharing of funny stories, this thread shall be used
for discussing death.

~~~~~~~~~~

As something of a NetHack newbie, I've made more than my share of
mistakes, and been unfairly killed my fair share of times.
Compulsively drinking from fountains just because they're there,
compulsively wearing rings, eating zombie corpses, shopping with
teleportitis, getting killed by a newt with an *identified, uncursed*
potion of extra healing in my inventory, attacking a freed djinn while
blind, and even getting hit on the head with a rock within the first
ten seconds-- I've done it all, it seems. However, my favorite (and
least favorite) story is also one that demonstrates how terrible I am
at the game.

The last time I really, really tried to power-play though the game
using all of my (very limited) spoiler knowledge, it was with (you
guessed it) a lawful human Valkyrie. I proceeded to get Excalibur and
descend to a non-random level, on Dlvl9, where, in the distance, I see
a tombstone next to a fountain.

Yeah.

Out of a narrow corridor comes not one, but two water demons. One
thrashes me to an inch of my life, at which point I pray for help, and
recieve it. Only with divine help am I able to kill one demon. There's
a staircase practically under my feet, but I'm not afraid-- I've got
Excalibur, and my weapon and armor are, after all, still enchanted.

Needless to say, the demon kills me.



